  "question": {
    "text": "A cell of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is connected across series combination of two resistors each of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistance. A voltmeter of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is used to measure the potential difference across each resistor. The reading of the voltmeter will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0114_31d67b4f9f79.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 198px;\" /></p><p>As we know,&nbsp;voltmeter is connected in parallel to the element being measured.</p><p>The equivalent resistance of the above circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Current through the circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>90</mn><mn>180</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Reading of the voltmeter is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  }
}